(root/'public/explore/explore.css').write_text(styles)
body=[]
for k,case in enumerate(j['cases']):
    pov=''.join(f'<article class="pov"><strong>{e(l["title"])}</strong><p><b>Priority:</b> {e(l["priority"])}</p><p><b>Possible benefit:</b> {e(l["potential_benefit"])}</p><p><b>Possible burden:</b> {e(l["potential_burden"])}</p><p><b>What evidence would help?</b> {e(l["question_to_test"])}</p><p class="small"><b>Child lens:</b> {e(l["child_lens"])}</p></article>' for l in case['perspectives'])
    branches=''.join(f'<article class="branch"><h4>{e(br["title"])}</h4><p><b>Potential benefit:</b> {e(br["potential_benefit"])}</p><p><b>Tradeoff:</b> {e(br["downside"])}</p><p><b>Dependency:</b> {e(br["critical_dependency"])}</p><p><b>Child future:</b> {e(br["child_future"])}</p><p><b>How to measure:</b> {e(br["observable_indicator"])}</p></article>' for br in case['branches'])
    cis=case['child_impact']
    body.append(f'''<details class="case" id="{e(case['id'])}" {'open' if k==0 else ''}><summary><span class="index">0{k+1}</span><span><span class="pill">FICTIONAL · {e(case['tag'])}</span><br><strong class="case-title">{e(case['title'])}</strong></span></summary><div class="case-body"><p>{e(case['question'])}</p><div class="note"><strong>Not a real project finding.</strong> These five lenses are fictional analytical viewpoints. The alternatives are unranked; no outcomes or probabilities have been established.</div><h3>Five points of view</h3><div class="povs">{pov}</div><h3>Alternative futures — none predetermined</h3><div class="branches">{branches}</div><h3>Child Impact Statement</h3><p><b>Past:</b> {e(cis['past'])}</p><p><b>Present:</b> {e(cis['present'])}</p><p><b>Future:</b> {e(cis['future'])}</p><p class="small">Source context for a real investigation: {e(' / '.join(case['source_context']))}. These are research starting points, not evidence for the fictional case.</p></div></details>''')
s='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><meta name="theme-color" content="#05082D"><meta name="description" content="Q-Pueblo research preview: public wiki methods, VISOR relations, regional shadow history, perspectives and child-first scenario learning."><title>Explore — Wiki, VISOR &amp; City Shadow | Q-Pueblo</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="./explore.css"></head><body><a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to research preview</a><header class="shell bar"><a class="brand" href="../index.html"><img src="../learn/brandmark.svg" alt="" width="66" height="66"><span><strong>Q-PUEBLO</strong><small>Know Pueblo. Help Shape Its Future.</small></span></a><nav aria-label="Explore navigation"><a href="../index.html">Home</a><a href="../learn/">Learn</a><a href="#wiki">Wiki</a><a href="#visor">VISOR</a><a href="#shadow">Shadow</a><a href="#scenarios">POV &amp; scenarios</a></nav></header>
<main class="shell" id="main"><div class="hero"><div><div class="eyebrow">RESEARCH PREVIEW · CONTROLLED CANDIDATE</div><h1>One Pueblo.<br>Many perspectives.<br><span style="color:#FFE7A3">Evolving evidence.</span></h1><p class="lead">A source-first way to learn, compare viewpoints, follow relationships and examine alternative futures without confusing a hypothesis with a fact.</p><div class="meta-row"><span class="tag">No personal profiles</span><span class="tag">No unreviewed allegation publication</span><span class="tag">Human-governed</span><span class="tag">Child Core · Past / Present / Future</span></div></div><div class="illustration" role="img" aria-label="Decorative Pueblo-inspired industrial landscape with mountain shapes, steel mill silhouette and river"><div class="sun"></div><div class="horizon"></div><div class="factory"></div><div class="river"></div></div></div>
<p class="call"><strong>Important:</strong> This is a demonstration of methods and user experience using fictional civic cases. It is not an operational city digital twin, a real GIS map, a verified release of historic case assertions, or a prediction of local outcomes. The actual reviewed Pueblo records will be connected only through future human-approved publication gates.</p>
<nav class="navcards" aria-label="Research sections"><a href="#wiki"><strong>📚 Wiki</strong><small>Definitions, sources and changing knowledge</small></a><a href="#visor"><strong>🔎 VISOR</strong><small>Who, what, relationships and evidence</small></a><a href="#shadow"><strong>🏙️ City Shadow</strong><small>Past, present, future at different scales</small></a><a href="#scenarios"><strong>🌿 Scenario Lab</strong><small>Five POVs, choices and child impact</small></a></nav>
<section class="section" id="wiki"><div class="eyebrow">01 · Q Wiki</div><h2>Read a claim. Inspect a source. Understand the version.</h2><p class="section-lead">A wiki entry is an explanation and a navigational layer, never its own primary evidence. It should link to original documents, counterevidence, review receipts, and earlier versions.</p><div class="grid2"><article class="card"><h3>Evidence grammar</h3><ul><li><b>Source:</b> an identifiable original or attributed record.</li><li><b>Claim:</b> a proposition with a date and evidence state.</li><li><b>Perspective:</b> an attributed interpretation, experience or concern.</li><li><b>Inference:</b> reasoning whose assumptions can be challenged.</li><li><b>Scenario:</b> an explicitly hypothetical alternative, not a forecast.</li><li><b>Outcome:</b> something actually observed and independently validated at an identified date.</li></ul></article><article class="card"><h3>Why a living wiki?</h3><p>The latest narrative must not silently erase what people knew before. Every correction should preserve the original claim, the reason for change, review authority, the superseded version and a new review/TTL trigger.</p><p class="small">A quote or screenshot is not automatically current or verified. Absence of evidence must remain UNKNOWN rather than FALSE.</p></article></div></section>
<section class="section" id="visor"><div class="eyebrow">02 · VISOR</div><h2>Explore relationships without making accusations.</h2><p class="section-lead">VISOR is a proposed evidence-linked graph, not a people-profiling tool. Each relationship needs a type, source, valid time, review and public-release approval.</p><div class="card"><div class="diagram" aria-label="Fictional example of an issue connected to a public institution and a project"><div class="node"><b>Fictional public issue</b><small>Issue / timeline</small></div><div class="node"><span class="arrow">⇄</span><p class="small">Evidence-linked relations<br>not judgments</p></div><div class="node"><b>Fictional project</b><small>Roles / cost stages</small></div></div><div class="scroll"><table class="method-table"><thead><tr><th>Relation</th><th>Meaning</th><th>What it does NOT prove</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Funds</td><td>A documented financial transaction at a stated stage</td><td>Misuse, repayment or effectiveness</td></tr><tr><td>Responsible agency</td><td>Statutory or contractual role with effective dates</td><td>Personal wrongdoing</td></tr><tr><td>Referenced by</td><td>Two records mention one another</td><td>Endorsement or actual control</td></tr><tr><td>Supersedes</td><td>A later record changes an earlier one</td><td>That the earlier record never existed</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></section>
<section class="section" id="shadow"><div class="eyebrow">03 · Regional City Shadow</div><h2>A time-indexed picture, not a claim of live omniscience.</h2><p class="section-lead">The eventual regional shadow can connect approved aggregates about transportation, public facilities, budgets and infrastructure over time. Household addresses, protected child locations and personal dossiers are excluded.</p><div class="grid2"><article class="card"><h3>Past → Present → Future</h3><p><b>Past:</b> archived source versions, remembered conditions and dated decisions.</p><p><b>Present:</b> approved observations with freshness indicators and unresolved gaps.</p><p><b>Future:</b> bounded possibilities, assumptions, intervals and triggers for review.</p></article><article class="card"><h3>Risk &amp; resource accounting</h3><p>Source publication, observation, event and approval timestamps stay separate. Financial amounts preserve requested/proposed/appropriated/contracted/paid/outcome stages. Energy, labor, attention and maintenance are measured when possible; otherwise UNKNOWN.</p><p class="small">No real-time feed or digital-twin validation is represented on this page.</p></article></div></section>
<section class="section" id="scenarios"><div class="eyebrow">04 · Multiple perspectives and evolving scenarios</div><h2>Learn to compare different truths people experience—and one evidentiary record.</h2><p class="section-lead">Explore four <b>fictional</b> case studies, each with five stakeholder lenses and three decision branches. These lenses are not quotes or positions of real officials, organizations or residents.</p><div class="cases">'''+''.join(body)+'''</div><p class="call"><strong>Quantum language:</strong> These branching futures are conventional scenario analysis, not quantum computation, probability claims, or proof that contradictory factual claims are equally supported.</p></section>
<section class="section" id="sources"><div class="eyebrow">05 · Source discovery</div><h2>Where to verify real Pueblo questions</h2><p>Start with controlling primary records. These are external discovery links and do not certify a specific issue.</p><ul class="sources"><li><a href="https://www.pueblo.us/1137/Council-Agenda" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">City of Pueblo council agendas</a> — meeting notices and governing documents</li><li><a href="https://pcclddigitalcollection.contentdm.oclc.org/digital/collection/p16620coll15" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Pueblo library digital newspaper archive</a> — historical primary sources</li><li><a href="https://www.pueblocounty.gov/planning-and-development-department/property-information-maps-online-services" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Pueblo County mapping portal</a> — public land and planning sources</li><li><a href="https://puebloura.org/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Pueblo Urban Renewal Authority</a> — authority and project information</li><li><a href="https://www.nist.gov/cyberframework" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">NIST Cybersecurity Framework</a> — defensive cybersecurity methods</li></ul></section></main>
<footer class="footer"><div class="shell"><strong>Q-Pueblo · Know Pueblo. Help Shape Its Future.</strong><p>Independent educational staging preview. No monitoring, accounts, community submissions, live GIS, predictive scores, official affiliation or publication of private research.</p><a href="../learn/">Return to the Learning Lab</a></div></footer></body></html>'''
(root/'public/explore/index.html').write_text(s)
print('Generated cases:',len(body),'HTML bytes:',len(s))
